  "material": {
    "_doc": "Liquid Glass roles. blur/saturate/brightness go to the compositor (backdrop); tint is painted on top and is neutral (glass has no colour of its own; it takes the backdrop's); rim is the 1px specular edge lit from the top left, edge the darker inner line on the far side (macOS 27), shine the top light catch (rimDark/rimLowDark/shineDark are the same over dark glass, where white light reads far stronger and has to stay faint), lens the width of the refracting band inside the rim. shadowY/shadowOpacity: the contact shadow. tinted/reduced: the tint's minimum opacity for the Tinted glass style and for Reduce Transparency. Roles: glassClear (shell over the wallpaper: Dock, widgets, lock screen), glassRegular (panels: Control Center, notifications, Spotlight, switcher), menu (menus and popovers: thicker, more opaque), glassControl (small controls on a window: toolbar groups, buttons, pop-up buttons), glassSidebar (window sidebars), glassDock (the Dock: smoked graphite, because on real GPUs the light clear tint reads as a bright white bar and washes out the icons).",
